      ],
      "selected_lines": [
        {
          "line": 49,
          "text": "## P13 \u2014 Docker cache and refresh improvements"
        },
        {
          "line": 50,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 51,
          "text": "**What:** Reuse package downloads and avoid invalidating security-refresh work unnecessarily during local source-only rebuilds, preserving upstream's release/security workflow."
        },
        {
          "line": 52,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 53,
          "text": "**Why:** Upstream already caches heavy dependency/model layers. The remaining donor benefits must be measured as deltas, not sold as a new cache architecture."
        },
        {
          "line": 54,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 55,
          "text": "**When:** W3 or earlier independently; no dependency on product features. Donors: `36636c4`, CPU `8fb396a`, CUDA `7063167`, Intel `bcda47f`."
        },
        {
          "line": 56,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 57,
          "text": "**Files / contract:** `.dockerignore`, affected Dockerfiles, minimal workflow/comment adjustments, `tests/test_docker_build_cache.py`, concise build documentation. Preserve current image names, architecture/provider choices and `SECURITY_REFRESH` behavior. Cache IDs separate incompatible CPU/Intel/CUDA package contexts. Do not copy training overlays or artifact/media directories into build contexts."
        },
        {
          "line": 58,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 59,
          "text": "- [ ] **E:** Record current cold build, local source-only rebuild with the same refresh argument, dependency change and forced refresh. Separately record CI's existing registry layer cache and per-run refresh argument; local mount reuse and cross-run CI persistence are different claims."
        },
        {
          "line": 60,
          "text": "- [ ] **S/I:** Port pip cache mounts and refresh-layer positioning only where they reduce work. Preserve dependency/model layers and explicit scheduled/release refreshes. Keep container caches out of final image contents."
        },
        {
          "line": 61,
          "text": "- [ ] **V:** Run `python -m pytest tests/test_docker_build_cache.py -q`, normal suite/build, and actual affected image builds with stage timings/layer evidence. Test source-only change and changed `SECURITY_REFRESH` separately; verify startup and model-provider registration."
        },
        {
          "line": 62,
          "text": "- [ ] **D:** Document builder/cache lifetime and which layers were reused. Docker documents that cache mounts live with the builder and are not automatically persisted in GitHub Actions cache; do not assume a mount survives fresh CI runners or add a new cache-workaround action without a demonstrated need. [Cache mounts](https://docs.docker.com/reference/dockerfile/#run---mounttypecache), [CI cache behavior](https://docs.docker.com/build/ci/github-actions/cache/)."
        },
        {
          "line": 63,
          "text": "- [ ] **R/L:** Submit a focused build PR, splitting CPU/Intel/CUDA only if they differ materially. Describe security refresh preservation and untested hardware explicitly; no release/version ownership changes."
        },
        {
          "line": 64,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 65,
          "text": "## P14 \u2014 Windows/NVIDIA inference setup"
        },
        {
          "line": 66,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 67,
          "text": "**What:** Preserve a small, working inference-only Compose/helper path and necessary GPU compatibility fixes."
        },
        {
          "line": 68,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 69,
          "text": "**Why:** A registered provider is not proof that the chosen plate model executes on the GPU; Windows path/context/build handoff can also fail independently of inference code."
        },
        {
          "line": 70,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 71,
          "text": "**When:** W3 once reproducible setup/hardware evidence exists; separate from P13 cache tuning. Donors: `9f63f6e`, narrowly selected `7c47815` changes."
        },
        {
          "line": 72,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 73,
          "text": "**Files / contract:** Appropriate existing Compose/deploy documentation, a small helper under `tools/` or the relevant platform directory only if needed, `tools/check_cuda.py`, focused tests under `tests/`. No training image or generated parallel inference Dockerfile."
        },
        {
          "line": 74,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 75,
          "text": "- [ ] **E:** Reproduce the actual daemon/context/path or provider issue on the target setup. Compare current upstream image requirements; do not restore an old ONNX Runtime pin just because the fork used it."
        },
        {
          "line": 76,
          "text": "- [ ] **I:** Keep the minimal inference configuration and explicit fallback/error behavior. Mock command construction/path handling in tests; never treat those mocks as GPU verification."
        },
        {
          "line": 77,
          "text": "- [ ] **V:** Build/run the supported image and execute an existing registered plate model on representative synthetic input with provider evidence. Check CPU behavior remains available and the chosen model/output agrees within justified tolerance."
        },
        {
          "line": 78,
          "text": "- [ ] **D/R/L:** PR material names OS, Docker/driver/provider/model versions, the original trigger and actual hardware exercised. If no suitable GPU/Windows environment is available, keep hardware verification outstanding rather than marking the task complete."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "path": ".superpowers/sdd/README/task-61-report.md",
